== probe 1: parser constraint discovery (8-byte cmdsize alignment) ==

fixture: minimal x86_64 MH_DYLIB, 5 commands, cmdsize values 4-aligned
(cmd 2 = LC_LOAD_DYLIB libbeta, cmdsize 68; 68 % 8 = 4).
command: PYTHONUTF8=1 rea trace-dylib-resolution probe.dylib --format json
exit: 1, stderr 0 bytes; body:
  {"error":"Analysis failed","code":"target_unavailable",
   "category":"unsupported_target",
   "message":"Cannot open artifact: load command 2 at offset 104 has invalid cmdsize 68.",
   "details":{"constraint":"file_format_rejected"}}
The 6.8.0 trace-dylib-resolution parser REQUIRES cmdsize % 8 == 0 in this
64-bit image (56 and 48, both % 8 == 0, were accepted in the same image
layout; 68 was rejected). The builder asserts 8-alignment per command and
records the constraint in its docstring.

